    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d195">

                <pb facs="0189" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg115"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-01"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 1, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 14th of
                    January, and to my reply of the 17th of January, relative to the movements of
                    the Sea King, or Shenandoah, and also to your note of the 14th of February,
                    relative to the movements of the Ajax, a copy of which latter note I
                    communicated to the lieutenant governor of Bermuda, I have the honor to transmit
                    to you a copy of a despatch which I have received from his excellency.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F.O. ADAMS, For Mr. BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d195-a1.xml" xpointer="d195-a1"/>
            </div>
